JavaScript is bundled; WASM is downloaded only at the user's request,
verified and cached in IndexedDB. No WASM or voice model is shipped in the ZIP.

Voice model weights are separate downloads, not covered by a blanket MIT
statement. Each voice has its own upstream MODEL_CARD with dataset/license
conditions, saved alongside the model. The settings link to that model card:
https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/tree/main/en/en_US/lessac/medium
https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/tree/main/en/en_GB/alba/medium
The test fixture uses the official rhasspy/piper v0.0.2 Lessac release.

Local implementation: src/neural-assets.js, src/neural-worker.js,
src/neural-speech.js, src/cloud-speech.js, src/tts-storage.js,
src/speech-voices.js and src/speech-settings.js. These source files and
package-lock.json are included for reproducible builds and modification.
The original eSpeak/speak.js notice and GPL comment remain unchanged.
